Yes.  The warning case is a bit more ambiguous as to what the game
"should" do.  Certainly, if you know that the behaviour is going to make
you lose a turn, then you can explicitly attack with the F + direction
key combination (Capital F, then the direction key as normal) to
explicitly attack a square rather than attempt to move into that square.

However if it appears that you know exactly where and what the monster
is, as is apparently the case with the detect monsters spell, then it
seems it should behave "correctly" and just attack rather than have the
"Wait!" behaviour.
